        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-21T23:08:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<blockquote><p><span>Sentinels of the Multiverse (SotM) is a collectible card game</span></p></blockquote><p><span>I'm not sure if you mean a \"cooperative card game\" as collectible card games are Magic the Gathering, Yu-Gi-Oh, etc.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>The only other thing a noticed is the division of cards. One-Shots, Persistant, and Power cards.</span></p><p><span>You list off Persistant cards as being \"Equipment, Ongoing, and Relic\". Relics in hero decks are also equipment cards. Powers are also listed on Ongoing or Equipment cards. Infact some cards even have persistant effects on the same cards that give a power. Such as Locallized Hurricane and&nbsp;Staff of Ra.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>Other than those few things, it looks great.</span></p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:46:53.199Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
