        "raw": "<blockquote><p><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-316e081a-036f-cd82-8b75-f650f602abf9\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; background-color: transparent;\">Sentinels of the Multiverse (SotM) is a collectible card game</span></p></blockquote><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; background-color: transparent;\">I&#39;m not sure if you mean a &quot;cooperative card game&quot; as collectible card games are Magic the Gathering, Yu-Gi-Oh, etc.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; background-color: transparent;\">The only other thing a noticed is the division of cards. One-Shots, Persistant, and Power cards.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; background-color: transparent;\">You list off Persistant cards as being &quot;Equipment, Ongoing, and Relic&quot;. Relics in hero decks are also equipment cards. Powers are also listed on Ongoing or Equipment cards. Infact some cards even have persistant effects on the same cards that give a power. Such as Locallized Hurricane and&nbsp;Staff of Ra.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; background-color: transparent;\">Other than those few things, it looks great.</span></p>",
